  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kvinna till Kvinna SPACE programme 2024-2025, Civil Society Strategy - Kvinna till Kvinna 2024 Strategy Civil Society</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kvinna till Kvinna, SPACE-programmet 2024-2025, CSO-strategin</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Sida f&#xf6;ljer upp insatsen p&#xe5; niv&#xe5;n &quot;CIVSAM Global Outcomes&quot;, till vilken resultat fr&#xe5;n landprogram och den regionala niv&#xe5;n f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntas bidra. &quot;CIVSAM Global Outcomes&quot; har f&#xf6;ljande 12 m&#xe5;l (WCSO&apos;s st&#xe5;r f&#xf6;r &quot;Women Civil Society Organizations&quot;). Notera att bed&#xf6;mningen &#xe4;r gjord p&#xe5; ett fem&#xe5;rigt resultatramverk. Inf&#xf6;r ett 11 m&#xe5;naders avtal har KtK justerat m&#xe5;len n&#xe5;got, vilket visar att KtK arbetar mot de fem&#xe5;riga m&#xe5;len, men kommer att kunna bidra till dem i mindre utstr&#xe4;ckning:

1. Feministisk fred

1a) Women&apos;s peacebuilding efforts have been successfully implemented, sustained, and have contributed to gendered conflict transformation.

(2024: Women&apos;s peacebuilding efforts have been strengthened)

1b) Women have documented and spread awareness about injustices and WCSO&apos;s have contributed to inclusive formal and informal justice frameworks.

(2024: Women have documented and spread awareness about injustices and WCSOs have contributed to build more inclusive formal and informal justice frameworks.)

1c) WCSO&apos;s advocacy related to the WPS agenda has influenced policy and practice.

(2024: WCSO&apos;s has conducted advocacy endeavours related to the WPS agenda to influence policy and practice.)

2. Politiska och ekonomiska r&#xe4;ttigheter

2a) Exclusionary structures and practices related to decision making on local, national and international levels have been challenged by WCSO&apos;s.

(2024: as above)

2b) Women maintain and/or increase their political participation in local and national governance structures.

(2024: Women have maintained and/or increased their political participation in elections as well as in local and national governance structures.)

2c) WCSO&apos;s and feminist initiatives have countered barriers to economic rights and justice, improving access to and control over resources.

(2024: WCSOs and feminist initiatives have advocated to remove barriers to economic rights and justice, to improve access to and control over resources.)

3. GBV och SRHR

3a) WCSO&apos;s advocacy lead to the improvement of legal frameworks, policies, and protection mechanisms of GBV survivors and SRHR right holders are improved and easily accessible.

(2024: WCSOs advocated for the improvement of legal frameworks, policies, and protection mechanisms of GBV survivors and SRHR.)

3b) Women&apos;s and girls&apos; access to safe healthcare services and justice at all levels has improved and access has increased.

(2024: Women&apos;s and girls&apos; access to  healthcare services has increased and justice at all levels has improved.)

3c) CSO&apos;s have challenged and/or contributed to the change of harmful social norms and attitudes related to gender, GBV and SRHR.

(2024: as above)

4. Feministiska r&#xf6;relser

4a) Dialogue and trust have increased between different women&apos;s rights groups bridging divisions and discrimination such as transphobia, age, disability, class, conflict narratives and other divides, contributing to a stronger and more inclusive womens movement.

(2024: as above)

4b) WCSO&apos;s joint actions have increased and have been acknowledged on local, national, and international levels.

(2024: WCSOs joint actions have increased)

4c) WCSO&apos;s have strengthened organisational capacity, improved security management and increased access to predictable, flexible and long-term financial support.

(2024: WCSOs have strengthened organisational capacity, improved security management and have fundraised and advocated for increased access to predictable, flexible and long-term financial support.)

Ut&#xf6;ver de m&#xe5;lniv&#xe5;er som ing&#xe5;r i avtalet med Sida, har resultatramverket &#xe4;ven m&#xe5;l p&#xe5; landniv&#xe5;.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kvinna till Kvinna (KtK) arbetar f&#xf6;r j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och kvinnors deltagande i fredsprocesser i l&#xe4;nder drabbade av krig och konflikt i linje med FN:s s&#xe4;kerhetsr&#xe5;dsresolution 1325 (och de efterf&#xf6;ljande resolutionerna om kvinnor, fred och s&#xe4;kerhetsagendan). KtK:s ans&#xf6;kan till Sida om st&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r programmet &quot;Strengthening Peacebuilders&apos; Actions for Community Engagement -&#xac; SPACE&quot; g&#xe4;llde &#xe5;ren 2024-2028. Detta avtal har tecknats p&#xe5; elva m&#xe5;nader p g a regeringens styrning till Sida i regleringsbrevet. Det har sedan f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngts t o m 30 september 2025 i enlighet med regeringens beslut om att m&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;ra en &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ngsfas.
Inom SPACE-programmet arbetar KtK med fyra tematiska f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringsomr&#xe5;den: 1) feministisk fred, 2) politiska och ekonomiska r&#xe4;ttigheter, 3) k&#xf6;nsrelaterat v&#xe5;ld (GBV) och sexuell, reproduktiv h&#xe4;lsa och r&#xe4;ttigheter (SRHR), och 4) feministiska r&#xf6;relser. KtK st&#xf6;djer dryga 60-talet lokala partnerorganisationer inom ramen f&#xf6;r SPACE-programmet i KtK:s fyra geografiska verksamhetsregioner: Afrika s&#xf6;der om Sahara, S&#xf6;dra Kaukasus och Ukraina, V&#xe4;stra Balkan samt Mellan&#xf6;stern och Nordafrika (MENA).
Programmet bed&#xf6;ms som relevant f&#xf6;r CSO-strategin 2024 och dess m&#xe5;lomr&#xe5;den 1) St&#xe4;rkt kapacitet hos civilsamh&#xe4;llet i utvecklingsl&#xe4;nder; och 2) F&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;ttningar f&#xf6;r civilsamh&#xe4;llesakt&#xf6;rer i utvecklingsl&#xe4;nder att verka.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Kvinna till Kvinna Foundation (KtK) works for gender equality and women&apos;s participation in peace processes in countries affected by war and conflict in line with UN Security Council Resolution 1325 (and the subsequent resolutions on the Women, Peace and Security Agenda). KtK&apos;s application to Sida for support for the program &quot;Strengthening Peacebuilders&apos; Actions for Community Engagement -&#xac; SPACE&quot; was for the years 2024-2028. This agreement has been signed for eleven months due to the government&apos;s steering to Sida in the appropriation direction. It has then been extended until September 30th 2025 following the government decision on possible extension in the new CSO strategy for 2025-2029. Within the SPACE program, KtK works with four thematic areas of change: 1) feminist peace, 2) political and economic rights, 3) gender-based violence (GBV) and sexual, reproductive health and rights (SRHR), and 4) feminist movements. KtK supports more than 60 local partner organizations within the framework of the SPACE program in KtK&apos;s four geographical operating regions: Sub-Saharan Africa, South Caucasus and Ukraine, Western Balkans, and Middle East and North Africa (MENA). The programme is assessed as relevant to the CSO Strategy 2024 and its target areas: 1) Strengthening the capacity of civil society in developing countries; and 2) Conditions for civil society actors in developing countries to operate.</narrative>
  </description>
